Verse 1:
[C]We [F/C]are [C]living, we [F/C]are [C]dwelling, In [F]a [Em]grand [C]and [Am]awful [C]time,
[G]In an [Em]age [Dm]on [G]ages [F#m]telling– [G]To be liv-ing is [C]sub-lime.
[G/D]Hark! [Dm]the [G]waking [C]up of nations, [F]Gog and [Dm]Magog to the fray;
[C]Hark! what [Am]soundeth? [G7/F]Is creation [G]Groaning [Dm]for her latter [G7]day?

Verse 2:
[C]Christian, rouse and arm [F/C]for [C]conflict, Nerve [F]thee [Em]for [C]the [Am]battlefield;
[G]Bear the [Em]helmet [G]of [C/E]salvation, [G]And the mighty gospel [C]shield;
[G/D]Let [Dm]the [G]breastplate, [C]peace, be on thee, [F]Take the [Dm]Spirit's sword in hand;
[C]Boldly, [Am]fearlessly, [G7/F]go [Em]forth then, [G]In [Dm]Jehovah's strength [C/G]to [G7]stand.

Verse 3:
[C]And [F/C]the [C]prince of evil spirits, Great [F]deceiver [Am]of [G]the [C]world!
[G]He [Em]who [Dm]at [G]the [C/E]blessed [F#m]Jesus [G]Once his deadly weapons [C]hurled,
[G/D]Cometh with [C]unwonted power, [F]Knowing [Dm]that his reign will cease
[C]When the [Am]kingdom [G7/F]shall be [Em]given [G]To [Dm]the mighty Prince [C/G]of [G7]Peace.

Verse 4:
[C]Christians, [F/C]rouse! [C]fight in this [F/C]warfare, [C]Cease not [F]till [Em]the [C]victory's won;
[G]Till your [Em]Captain [G]loud [C/E]proclaimeth, [G]"Servant of the Lord, [C]well done!"
[G/D]He, [Dm]alone, [C]who thus is faithful, [F]Who abideth [Dm]to the end,
[C]Hath the [Am]promise, [G7/F]in the [Em]kingdom [G]An [Dm]eternity [C/G]to [G7]spend.
